## Deliverable and sources

Create [a new plotting script](../../notebooks/plot_guardian_period_comparison.py) and an isolated [output folder](../../output/guardian_period_comparison_findings/) containing combined and standalone tone/coverage PDF, 600 dpi PNG and editable-text SVG exports, plus a README with source selectors, reproduction command, caption and verification evidence.

- Tone means: [a1_age30_levels.csv](../../data/dataset_nlp/results/a1_age30_levels.csv), RoBERTa before/after mean columns only. Main n, changes and test: [a1_age30_results.csv](../../data/dataset_nlp/results/a1_age30_results.csv), RoBERTa/main. Ignore the unverified historical between-age interval.
- Coverage medians: [a1_coverage_age.csv](../../data/dataset_nlp/results/a1_coverage_age.csv), all article types, season only, before/after median columns. This is a descriptive count display; do not reuse the modelled ratios as arithmetic article ratios.
- Style: [PLOTTING_STYLE.md](../../PLOTTING_STYLE.md), with 17.8 cm combined width from the supplied PNAS template. Older orange circles, younger dark-brown squares; readable labels; no uncertainty bars or signed-score percentage changes. Tone uses 67/753 signings; coverage uses 88/1,244 including zeros.

## Course connection and pending selection

The saved [Week 7 sentiment section](<../../../data/week7/Week 7 · From meaning to measurement · 02805.html#sentiment>) motivates measuring change over time and illustrates sentiment trajectories with smoothing across a narrative. That supports the user's preference for a temporal view. A signing-centred monthly arc is this project's adaptation; the course example does not validate the covariate adjustment in the existing H2b plot. Discuss which comparison the eventual paper figure needs to communicate, keeping monthly descriptive trajectories distinct from the tested signing-level period changes.

## Verification and completion criteria

Match plotted values and denominators to saved source rows. Check input hashes and unchanged historical PDF hashes. Inspect rendered combined and standalone PDFs at final physical size and in grayscale; verify embedded fonts, rotation, dimensions, vector output and absence of clipped or overlapping labels. Keep captions explicit about windows, sentence filtering, equal signing weight, separate samples and missing uncertainty intervals. Record produced/verified artifacts separately from the user's eventual figure choice.

Resolve when the user confirms satisfaction with the produced comparison or explicitly declines it after inspection. Return the Figure 2 choice and any layout/caption consequences to Issue 09, the storyline and checkpoint. Issue 09 remains open meanwhile.

